@using ContentManagementSystem.Rendering.Navigation
@using ContentManagementSystem.Rendering.Seo
@* The whole HTML document a public request receives. Static SSR only: there is no @@rendermode
   anywhere beneath this, no blazor.web.js, and no circuit — which is the decision that makes the
   response cacheable at all (spec section 5.3).

   Deliberately hand-written rather than reusing App.razor. App.razor is the backoffice's shell and
   carries the WebAssembly bootstrapper and the ImportMap; serving that to an anonymous reader would
   download the editor to every visitor and undo the reason the two front doors are separate. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
@* lang comes from SiteSettings.Culture, resolved on the same settings read the head already makes
   (spec section 28, task P9-10). A screen reader chooses its pronunciation from this, so a wrong or
   absent value is a failure nobody sees and every listener hears. *@
<html lang="@Seo.Language">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <CmsSeoHead Metadata="Seo" Context="Context" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css" />
</head>
<body>
@* The site's primary navigation belongs to the shell rather than to a template: it is the same on
   every page by definition, and a template that had to render it would be a template that can
   forget to. It takes a nav:*tree cache dependency on this render, so publishing anywhere in the
   tree evicts every page showing it (task P8-17). *@
<CmsNavigation Context="Context" Label="Main" />
<main class="cms-delivery">
    <CmsPageHost Context="Context" />
</main>
</body>
</html>
